<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 59,786 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 59,786 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 59,786 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 71,759 tonnes on Thursday.</p>
<p>Officials at the port said no report was made for cargo handling on Saturday because of an anti-government strike by opposition parties against new taxes.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 5,548	    7,271</p>
<p>    Import cargo			54,238	   64,488</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Mirinda  26/10</p>
<p>Jet fuel		 25,000	 Chilham Castle   29/10</p>
<p>Sugar		     1,400	 Gemstar-1	  26/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Courage  22/10</p>
<p>Jute			4,187	 Banglar Kiran	due</p>
<p>Jute			5,419	 Al-Salma	     due</p>
<p>Sulphur		   5,000	 Calimenesti	  due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
